{
  "_about": [
    "Which migration files are live on the platform database. Merged is not applied: a file counts as applied only after its objects were probed live.",
    "Every file in supabase/migrations must appear here exactly once (tests/unit/migrations/migration-status.test.ts). A new migration is added to `applied` once it is applied AND probed, or to `notApplied` with the condition it is waiting for.",
    "The live ledger (supabase_migrations.schema_migrations) uses its own version numbers because migrations are applied through the Supabase MCP, so match by name and probe the objects, never by version.",
    "`npm run db:status` prints everything that is not fully live."
  ],
